#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0047 expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "PLAN-occds-source-domain-by-ig D4 as sharpened by its review H1, on OUR metadata store: an ADAE declared OCCDS (as by a define's def:Class) that carries NO occurrence variable (no --SEQ, --TERM, --TRT or --DECOD; AEBODSYS is not evidence) resolves against the D10-inferred OCCDS 1.0 (base Req STUDYID, USUBJID, --SEQ, --TERM, CMTRT, AESER). With no evidence of any domain the '--' names stay unresolved and are not demanded, and NO concrete carried name is dropped - an empty evidence set never disarms a requirement - so CMTRT and AESER are both demanded and both absent -> one violation naming [CMTRT, AESER]. A variant that dropped every carried name not in the (empty) evidence set would leave this dataset silent."
#library-ref standard=adamig version=1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt "$missing_required_variables"="[CMTRT, AESER]"
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AEBODSYS type=Char label="Body System or Organ Class"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | NERVOUS SYSTEM DISORDERS
---
